# Build-time environment for a split deployment (frontend on Cloudflare Pages,
# backend on Render/Railway).
#
# Copy to `.env.production` for a one-off local build, or — preferably — set
# VITE_API_BASE_URL in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard so the value is not
# committed.  Vite inlines this variable at build time: changing the backend
# URL requires a new frontend build.
#
# Must be the absolute API origin INCLUDING the /api/v1 prefix and no trailing
# slash, otherwise the browser will call the Pages host and get a 404.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://lakewatch-api.onrender.com/api/v1

# Local development does not need this file: the Vite dev server proxies
# /api and /health to http://localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts).
